        "original_id": "12457b8c-0c24-5b4a-9fd5-ec56fcec0e11",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dave Faulkner, Richard Grossman, Mark Kingsmill, Brad Shepherd, Pierre Bouvier\n- Music Groups: Hoodoo Gurus, Simple Plan\n- Albums: Electric Soup, Electric Soup: The Singles Collection\n- Places: Sydney, Australia, Canada\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, guitarist, bassist, drummer, harmonica player, composer, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Hoodoo Gurus are an Australian rock band formed in Sydney in 1981.\n- Dave Faulkner formed Hoodoo Gurus and was the band’s mainstay as songwriter, lead singer, and guitarist.\n- Richard Grossman later joined Hoodoo Gurus as bassist, Mark Kingsmill later joined as drummer, and Brad Shepherd later joined as guitarist, vocalist, and harmonica player.\n- Electric Soup, also known as Electric Soup: The Singles Collection, is the first compilation album by Hoodoo Gurus.\n- By September 1992, Electric Soup contained all Hoodoo Gurus Australian singles released up to that date.\n- Pierre Charles Bouvier was born on 9 May 1979.\n- Pierre Bouvier is a Canadian singer, songwriter, musician, composer, and actor.\n- Pierre Bouvier is best known as the lead singer and guitarist of the rock band Simple Plan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
